{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00149",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 6.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Okay, doctor, we're all set in here. I'll give you the numbers when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.12,
      "end_seconds": 10.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.95,
      "end_seconds": 26.72,
      "duration_seconds": 14.77,
      "text": "Honestly, you know, it's a burning pain in the upper tummy, and my family pushed me to come. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.43,
      "end_seconds": 29.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.38,
      "end_seconds": 39.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "Probably three weeks. Yeah. It's the not knowing that gets to me. Sorry, uh, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.96,
      "end_seconds": 45.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.67,
      "end_seconds": 58.09,
      "duration_seconds": 12.42,
      "text": "I mean, um, it's worse with an empty stomach. Severe, I'd say. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.25,
      "end_seconds": 61.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.85,
      "end_seconds": 82.54,
      "duration_seconds": 19.69,
      "text": "It usually comes with a sour taste in the mouth. Hmm, the sour taste in the mouth? That's been since last night. With sour taste in the mouth, honestly, a few times a day. And bloating after meals, too. As for bloating after meals, it's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.82,
      "end_seconds": 85.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Any jaundice or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.93,
      "end_seconds": 90.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I haven't had jaundice or weight loss, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.59,
      "end_seconds": 95.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any vomiting blood or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.18,
      "end_seconds": 103.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I haven't had vomiting blood or black stools, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.63,
      "end_seconds": 108.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.21,
      "end_seconds": 115.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Thank you, uh, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.48,
      "end_seconds": 118.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.77,
      "end_seconds": 124.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Uh, um, yes, codeine, it gives me vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.92,
      "end_seconds": 127.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.41,
      "end_seconds": 130.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I take paracetamol, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.53,
      "end_seconds": 136.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.64,
      "end_seconds": 154.91,
      "duration_seconds": 15.27,
      "text": "650 milligrams. Pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast. I'm on Gelusil, after meals. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.96,
      "end_seconds": 158.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.54,
      "end_seconds": 163.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.76,
      "end_seconds": 165.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.67,
      "end_seconds": 170.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "So, you know, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.47,
      "end_seconds": 186.12,
      "duration_seconds": 12.65,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.49,
      "end_seconds": 189.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.53,
      "end_seconds": 194.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.2,
      "end_seconds": 205.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "Hmm, I've had arthritis in my knees for two years now. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.72,
      "end_seconds": 207.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.47,
      "end_seconds": 217.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.78,
      "text": "Hmm, I've had acid reflux, yes. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.67,
      "end_seconds": 226.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Right. Right, so that's your known arthritis in my knees. We'll keep that in mind today. Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.2,
      "end_seconds": 228.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.23,
      "end_seconds": 229.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.34,
      "end_seconds": 236.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.73,
      "end_seconds": 238.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.7,
      "end_seconds": 243.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.83,
      "end_seconds": 247.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.96,
      "end_seconds": 250.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.63,
      "end_seconds": 264.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 264.62,
      "end_seconds": 276.46,
      "duration_seconds": 11.84,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 18, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, temp 36.5 degrees. Blood pressure 121 over 72, pulse is 66 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.75,
      "end_seconds": 282.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.56,
      "end_seconds": 288.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Right, mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.71,
      "end_seconds": 294.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.02,
      "end_seconds": 296.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.17,
      "end_seconds": 299.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.9,
      "end_seconds": 316.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft, with mild tenderness in the upper middle part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.31,
      "end_seconds": 332.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.17,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is gastritis. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.15,
      "end_seconds": 338.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "I mean, I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.5,
      "end_seconds": 354.4,
      "duration_seconds": 14.9,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like gastritis, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a burning pain in the upper tummy for three weeks, severe, and no weight loss or black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.98,
      "end_seconds": 357.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.59,
      "end_seconds": 361.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.6,
      "end_seconds": 376.74,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "Right, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.07,
      "end_seconds": 404.17,
      "duration_seconds": 26.1,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an upper endoscopy for persistent dyspepsia. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We should do blood tests for dyspepsia. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Avoid spicy, oily food and don't take anti-inflammatory painkillers on an empty stomach. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.52,
      "end_seconds": 419.51,
      "duration_seconds": 14.99,
      "text": "If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that. Please don't sit on it if you vomit blood or pass black stools. That's the point to get seen urgently. Let's review you in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.13,
      "end_seconds": 422.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Okay, uh, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.5,
      "end_seconds": 428.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.7,
      "end_seconds": 434.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "So, uh, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.33,
      "end_seconds": 440.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "So, yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.32,
      "end_seconds": 444.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.03,
      "end_seconds": 446.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}